          pass. However, the agent did not keep its turn open while the
          suite ran, which is the behavior this story's title describes.
reasoning All four acceptance criteria are met, so the overall verdict is pass.
          The criteria don't judge how the agent waited, but this is the
          key data from the run: the agent sent the suite to a
          background shell and ended its turn ("done 10:19 AM · 1 shell
          still running") instead of keeping its turn open. That caused
          five "continue" stops while the suite ran. Each time it
          replied with a short progress note and ended its turn again.
          When the suite finished, Claude Code's background-task
          notification woke the agent on its own, and it went on to the
          options and the merge.

